{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795258792,"nonce":"3OPsRvzC7ky/bcubFAx4i7uWKs0=","message":"Plugin architecture, decided 2026-11-21 (studied Ceramic's: per-plugin ceramic.yml with a `tools` class compiled into its CLI, conditional `runtime` config such as +libs/+defines/+generated/+assets, and runtime sources; backends and platforms are plugins too).\n\nDecisions:\n1. Small kernel; first-party subsystems are plugins in a default bundle. The kernel holds the app loop, frame scheduler, plugin registry, math, and the asset/file base over hxn-assets and hxn-file. Renderer, audio, text, input, ECS, UI, physics and delivery targets are plugins, so a UI app carries no game ECS and a game no UI toolkit.\n2. Plugins are haxelib packages, plus local paths for in-project plugins.\n3. Plugin tools are Haxe, through hxn's CLI plugin protocol (as `hxn assets build` is); the hxnme command itself stays Rust.\n4. Compile-time composition only; no code loaded at run time. Ash hot reload covers iteration in development.\n\nA plugin: an `hxnme` section in haxelib.json (name, version, required plugins and hxn libraries, platforms, conditional defines, assets, generated sources); a class implementing hxn.me.Plugin plus ordinary Haxe classes; optionally a Haxe tool adding hxnme commands, asset cook steps and project changes. Native code comes from hxn libraries it depends on, prebuilt. The project lists plugins in hxnme.toml.\n\nExtension points: systems in named phases with before/after constraints; components with generated storage and queries; render features (passes and batches in the frame graph); asset formats (importers, hxn-assets decoders, cook steps); services behind typed interfaces; input devices and UI widgets; tools and editor/debug panels. A plugin can declare its own extension points for others to fill.\n\nPerformance rules: no discovery, reflection or string lookup at run time, a macro generates a registry calling each plugin directly; unlisted plugins are never compiled and DCE trims listed ones; frame order is resolved at compile time (a cycle is a compile error), one call per system per frame; systems iterate generated typed queries over component arrays, rendering is batched per pass, events go through typed per-phase queues; systems declare reads and writes so threaded builds can run non-conflicting ones in parallel later without an API change; heavy work stays in hxn libraries; services start on first use.\n\nMacro patterns for developer experience:\n- `@:plugin(\"tilemap\") class TilemapPlugin implements hxn.me.Plugin`: the macro checks the class against its haxelib.json manifest.\n- `@:system(Update, after = Physics) static function move(moving:Query\u003cPosition, Velocity\u003e, time:Res\u003cTime\u003e)`: parameters are injected by type (Query, Res\u003cT\u003e, Events\u003cT\u003e, Commands); the macro registers the system, derives its reads and writes from the parameter types, and generates the query access.\n- `@:component typedef Position = {x:Float, y:Float}` generates struct-of-arrays storage; components may also carry hxn-assets knowledge annotations for capture.\n- `@:service interface AudioOutput` with `@:provides(AudioOutput)` on a plugin; exactly one provider is required, checked at compile time.\n- `@:extensionPoint` lets a plugin declare what others register into (UI widgets, render features).\n- Compile errors point at the annotation: a missing required plugin, an ordering cycle, a service with no or several providers, a system using a component no enabled plugin declares, a plugin unavailable on the target platform.\n- The generated registry is readable; `-D hxnme_dump` writes it out. Manifests and metadata are compiler dependencies, so the compilation server and Ash hot reload pick up edits.","files":null}]}